Z||000004||Oreif||11-07-2000||12:27 PM||||Haze, Is this on the 87 SE? Did it run prior to pulling the distributor? Are you sure you didn't switch 2 spark plug wires? White/grey smoke could be oil if it has a blue tint. Does it smell like burnt oil or antifreeze? Antifreeze is white. I have a Pontiac Service manual if you need it. (It's an 86 but there are very minor differences between 86 and 87) If you need any help let me know.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||11-07-2000||12:33 PM||||Never saw a pig that smoked... Wait - that's what happens to nicotine-addicted porkers, I guess?  They use them for smoked ham  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.<P>Back to more serious matters.  First, make sure you're setting the timing using the correct slot on the damper (there are three on mine).  Might pull some plugs and see if you've got coolant in there (hope not!). ||||reg||5
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||11-07-2000||12:48 PM||||Oreif.....<BR>Yes its the 87.. I didnt remove any wires. It smells like normal exhaust.. No blue tint or anything.<P>StuGood.....<BR>So I could have put the Dis. in wrong.. Huh? I did chech the dipstick. Oils dirty but no water.<P>????????????????????????????????????????????<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">   <BR>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD"<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 11-07-2000).]||||reg||9
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||11-07-2000||01:33 PM||||Ok ... so I came in to calm down and get a drink. Now when I start it theres no smoke for about 8-9sec. Then out it comes. At first the rpm's are high (Like all Fiero's + Its cold out) 10 sec's into it the car hesitates BAD. And I hearing engine noises. Lots of clicking and clanking. Not a rod noise or anything like that. I guess im not sure what it should sound like. When I test drove it the Alt. was bad and the mounting bolt was broke. <P><BR>I ordered pulgs - cap - rotor & 8mm wires from the Fiero Store. I guess Ill have to wait untill they get here and do a tune up. Ill probley have to replace the damn Dis. to.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">  <BR>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD"||||reg||8
Z||000008||ThatRickGuy||11-07-2000||02:12 PM||||could it just be retarded to much? if it starts fine maybe the comp is trying cold start or what ever, but once it tries to drop to low idle it could be droping too far back... Try starting it in diagnostic mode, use a paper clip to short out the 1st 2 pegs on the lower passanger side of the computer hook up under the cig lighter cover. might be worth a try. That should eliminate any computer problems, which is the only thing that I could imagine would cause it to suddenly mess up the idle, unless there's some kinda of screwy head gasket leak. You won't always be able to see the coolant on the dip stick if it is a head gasket leak tho, so it maybe a wise idea to go ahead w/ an oil change.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||11-07-2000||02:26 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ThatRickGuy:<BR><B>could it just be retarded to much? if it starts fine maybe the comp is trying cold start or what ever, but once it tries to drop to low idle it could be droping too far back... Try starting it in diagnostic mode, use a paper clip to short out the 1st 2 pegs on the lower passanger side of the computer hook up under the cig lighter cover. might be worth a try. That should eliminate any computer problems, which is the only thing that I could imagine would cause it to suddenly mess up the idle, unless there's some kinda of screwy head gasket leak. You won't always be able to see the coolant on the dip stick if it is a head gasket leak tho, so it maybe a wise idea to go ahead w/ an oil change.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>At this point Ill give anything a try..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>Carl<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">  <BR>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD"||||reg||8
Z||000010||theogre||11-07-2000||07:36 PM||||It's pulling coolant into it someplace.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Indiana_resto_guy||11-07-2000||11:18 PM||||C,<P>Just for fun, double check rotor placement I think you dropped it in a tooth off. I know that it ran fine when you got it and it's not been on the street yet, so it can''t be anything drastic. Didn't break or pull off any vacumn lines did you? (EGR?)<BR>Have a chance to trouble shoot the lights yet?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Haze_Performance||11-08-2000||09:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B>C,<P>Just for fun, double check rotor placement I think you dropped it in a tooth off. I know that it ran fine when you got it and it's not been on the street yet, so it can''t be anything drastic. Didn't break or pull off any vacumn lines did you? (EGR?)<BR>Have a chance to trouble shoot the lights yet?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I didnt break any lines.. And the computer has no codes. The dash light is off. Im going to replace the Dis. + a tune up next.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlogo1_1.gif">  <BR>"AHHHHH!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD"||||reg||10
Z||000013||ThatRickGuy||11-08-2000||10:31 AM||||an oil change is cheeper then a new distributer, and will let you know for sure if there's a blown head gasket or other leak. If there's nothing in the oil, then I'd say re-drop the distributer, if it is one tooth off that would cause missing, sputtering, maybe some backfiring and the like. but again, it's cheeper then new parts.||||reg||1
